## Context
Some extracted CSVs contain only a header row and no data (e.g.,
census/gpt-5-mini-run{1,2,3}, census/gpt-5-nano-run{1,2,3},
census/grok-4.20-run3). When the evaluate pipeline processes these,
cleaner.py:75 raises ValueError("The input DataFrame is empty."),
crashing the parallel make and blocking measurement assembly.

Currently worked around with `-k` flag in Makefile (ticket 0036),
but the proper fix is to return a ResultSummary(status="error")
for empty CSVs instead of crashing.

## Actions
1. In evaluate.py, catch the empty DataFrame error from cleaner
2. Return ResultSummary(status="error") with a descriptive message
3. Remove the `-k` workaround from Makefile once the crash is fixed

## Test
Write a test with a header-only CSV → expect status="error" record.

## Exit criteria
- `make -C experiments rebuild-measurements` completes without `-k`
- Empty CSVs produce error records instead of crashes
